															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/novaedearx" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1310897); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1310897&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608973932" alt="NovaeDeArx" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1310897)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/novaedearx" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1310897); return false;" >NovaeDeArx</a></span> <span class="odate time_1431005947 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">07 May 2015 13:39</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2287892">
									

<p>Which was pretty much what saved it for me&#8230; I spent most of the time thinking &quot;Gosh, that's a hell of a lot of money and time and resources spent on brain-chipping and brainwashing death-row inmates.&quot;</p>
<p>Making them an unwitting panopticon justifies the cost, and there's always room to play with the brain implant. Maybe it's what the good doctor says it is, maybe he's lying, maybe he thinks he knows what it is but he's wrong.</p>
<p>I'm often annoyed when people try to retcon the D-Class termination, because it means one of a few things:<br />
-We're taking mercy on death-row inmates by&#8230; What, returning them to prison where the state will kill them instead? Returning them to society where at least some portion of them will violently reoffend?<br />
-D-Class aren't really &quot;people&quot;, but clones or something. Oh, great. Now we're either neutering the horror (if they're non-sapient) or unintentionally creating a whole new set of ethical issues (mass-producing innocent, sapient lives with the express intention of killing them) to try to work around killing some of the worst individuals in our society instead. Um&#8230;<br />
-We're dumping hundreds or thousands of people a month back into society (regardless of their actual source) that have potentially been affected by SCP objects. Oh, yeah. That'll end well. Not to mention that it massively clashes with at least two of the basic tenets of the Foundation (Secure, Contain).<br />
-We're mind-wiping the D-Class at the end of every month and returning them to circulation. Either that means we're cross-contaminating SCP objects or the D-Class are being returned to the same objects, which will probably kill them eventually anyhow. It's pretty much the same problem as the monthly terminations, except now we're kicking it down the line indefinitely.</p>
<p>I don't know if someone has yet come up with a plausible, alternate explanation to a monthly termination. Yours is one of the better ones, but it still has the problem of &quot;But some of these folks WILL have SCP object contamination&#8230; What about Secure &amp; Contain?&quot; as mentioned above. Overall, though, not bad.</p>

							</div>

								
					
