			<div class="content" id="post-content-2288179">
									

<blockquote>
<p>Hey, the USA has the highest (recorded!) prison population per capita of any industrialized nation IRL</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Note that's only <strong>recorded</strong>, and doesn't include developing nations.</p>
<p>Regardless, assuming a typical Safe/Euclid site houses 10-15 SCPs, and providing two D-class per SCP for testing (one active and one in reserve), that site would eat up between 240 and 360 D-class <em>per year</em>. And if this holds true for sites accross the board, we're talking a minimum of 24,960 to 37,440 D-class <em>per year</em>. Note that only 56 countries still have the Death Penalty, out of about 200.</p>
<p>The figures assume that (more or less) all D-class survive to termination, that no SCP needs more than one D-class active for testing purposes, and that Areas do NOT use D-class. If any of those are wrong, then the numbers would become significantly higher than my estimate. For that level of use to be accurate, the Foundation would basically need to live in a <em>Judge Dredd</em> style dystopia where capital punishment-level crime is commonplace.</p>

							</div>

								
