					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/sirpudding" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(348648); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=348648&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608973932" alt="sirpudding" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=348648)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/sirpudding" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(348648); return false;" >sirpudding</a></span> <span class="odate time_1431028462 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">07 May 2015 19:54</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2288152">
									

<blockquote>
<p>-We're taking mercy on death-row inmates by… What, returning them to prison where the state will kill them instead? Returning them to society where at least some portion of them will violently reoffend?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The default is that we are executing a bunch of political refugees unless we give them a special per-person monthly wavier. The vast majority of D-Class have to be refugees, there simply aren't enough people awaiting execution to make up the required numbers.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>-We're mind-wiping the D-Class at the end of every month and returning them to circulation. Either that means we're cross-contaminating SCP objects or the D-Class are being returned to the same objects, which will probably kill them eventually anyhow. It's pretty much the same problem as the monthly terminations, except now we're kicking it down the line indefinitely.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>It <em>does</em> solve the volume problem, which is pretty significant.</p>

							</div>

								
					
